:name: interactive execution profile
:description: fast, for the edit loop. NOT bit-reproducible - see ci.resc

# Design section 4.3 defines two execution profiles, and until now neither was selectable: every
# scenario hard-coded these two lines, so rules G1 and G2 (section 9.2) applied to nothing.
#
# quantum 2 ms is the largest quantum that keeps firmware output byte-identical. It is a CORRECTNESS
# parameter, not a performance one: at 5 ms the firmware loses roughly 2.5% of its counter periods
# with no error message, and the error is duration-dependent - 5 ms looks right at 5 and 10 virtual
# seconds and only breaks at 20. Do not raise it to go faster.
emulation SetGlobalQuantum "0.002"

# Removes Renode's real-time throttle, which otherwise caps the emulation at exactly 1.0x.
# Measured on an 8-core x86-64 host: 4.50x real time with four nodes.
#
# The cost is reproducibility. Runs under this profile diverge in internal state, and the tail of a
# RunFor boundary can move by a line. Assertions written against this profile must match on content,
# never on line count.
emulation SetGlobalAdvanceImmediately true
